Subject: [PATCH 0012/0014] Server runtime configuration

No upstream code changes are needed for the workspace runtime
contract, so this patch carries no hunks (build.sh skips diff-less
patches explicitly). The stock server already satisfies every clause:

- Loopback only: --host defaults to localhost; our guest unit passes
  --host 127.0.0.1 explicitly.
- Data folder: --server-data-dir (defaults under the server data
  folder name from patch 0001).
- Socket path: --socket-path exists; we serve TCP loopback because
  the gateway reaches the guest over vsock TCP forwarding.
- Session handshake: the signed JWT session is verified by the
  gateway on every connection (see gateway JwtVerifier); the
  connection-token flags exist for operators who terminate TLS
  ahead of the gateway.

The guest unit base-image-builder/systemd/jahaziel-code-server.service
launches bin/jahaziel-code-server (the packaged name follows
serverApplicationName from patch 0001) with --without-connection-token
on loopback: with no route-push transport yet there is no channel for
a per-workspace token, so the gateway JWT check plus vsock-only
ingress is the auth boundary. Switching the unit to
--connection-token-file is the defined seam once route push lands.

Touches: (contract only; guest unit lives in base-image-builder/)

Verification: server boot smoke test inside a workspace VM.
